+/**
+ * Install-step (pimLoop subclass) that runs self-extracting-executable (SFX)
+ * payloads as child processes -- PTC's alternative to MSI for products/
+ * utilities packaged as a plain .exe installer.
+ *
+ * Responsibilities:
+ * - Iterate <SFX install="Y"> elements and launch each referenced executable.
+ * - Interpret the child process's exit code using the same well-known Windows
+ *   Installer exit-code vocabulary as pimMSILoop (many SFX payloads are
+ *   themselves MSI-based). Exit code 1618 is deliberately handled differently
+ *   here (treated as failure) than in pimMSILoop (treated as cancellation).
+ * - Support cooperative termination via a mutex-guarded kill_exec flag,
+ *   polled every 2 seconds while the child process runs.
+ * - Append a successful package's uninstall command line to a shared
+ *   Uninstall_all_utilities.bat file, keyed by product mode.
+ *
+ * Dependencies:
+ * - pimLoop (base class).
+ * - btkProcess (external btk) for child-process creation/monitoring.
+ * - pimConvert for property-placeholder resolution.
